2026-04-02T20:30:00 — NEEDS REVIEW: spellStackDistinctCasters invariant too strict
  Seeds: 0x1e4e0cea, 0xaa35cc2c, 0x2e7721b6, 0x42b324d5, 0xfc289896, 0xd4a42686
  The invariant requires all spell stack entries to have distinct casterIds.
  But SRD allows: A casts fireball → D counterspells → A counter-counterspells.
  This creates stack with caster A at positions 1 and 3 — violating the invariant.
  This is legal per SRD: counterspell is a reaction, and the original caster can
  use their reaction to counter a counterspell targeting their spell.
  Fix options:
    a) Remove spellStackDistinctCasters from allBattleInvariants (with comment)
    b) Weaken to: adjacent stack entries have distinct casters (no self-counter)
    c) Weaken to: only non-counterspell entries must have distinct casters
  SRD rule: "Casting in Response" / Counterspell — PHB spell description.
  Recommend option (b) or (c). Human judgment needed on which invariant is correct.

